From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristjan Sillmann <kristjan.h.s@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:39:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pc-voice

vic-anim TTS provider (B4.2, R15-R18): each line reads /data/data/myvector-voice.json
{url, voice, slow}; missing/bad file, no url or voice stock speaks Acapela unchanged. Otherwise
each sentence is one HTTP/1.0 POST /tts to the PC service (slow = file slow x durationScalar,
clamped 0.5-2.0; 1.5 s to the first response byte, 20 s and 4 MB for the whole sentence), its
16 kHz PCM resampled to Acapela's rate because a stream keeps its first chunk's rate. Chunk
sizes are bounded before any size_t sum (32-bit wrap). A failed sentence and the rest of the
line speak in Acapela (R17). Logs my-vector.Voice. Host test: robot/firmware/tests/pc-voice.sh.

R19: SDK SayText (wire-pod) stays Acapela: sdkComponent sets the new TextToSpeechPrepare.sdkOrigin, vic-anim passes it to the provider, which skips the PC voice (log 'acapela: sdk SayText (R19)'). Built-in lines (time, weather, behaviours) keep T2.
B5: the KnowledgeGraph response line (wire-pod's streaming placeholder) also sets sdkOrigin via BehaviorTextToSpeechLoop::SetTextToSay - PC voice put +0.5-0.64 s before its first sound, PC down +1.5 s.

Unprocessed: a line the PC voice starts plays with the Unprocessed switch, not the line's Default_Processed - that robot-voice effect made the PC voice sound robotic on built-in lines (time, weather). A line that falls back to Acapela at its first sentence keeps its style; a later-sentence fallback plays unprocessed.
